on","entry_id":"guide-entry-6fab373d13731dea6f25338d","section":"other"},"guide-entry-cebb17607a4b326a6467ed86":{"description":"Report of the International Law Commission on the work of its twenty-fourth session, 2 May to 7 July 1972 Established a Working Group to review the problem and prepare a set of draft articles. On the basis of the reports of the Working Group, the Commission adopted a set of 12 draft articles, with commentaries , on the prevention and punishment of crimes against diplomatic agents and other internationally protected persons, which it submitted to the Assembly as well as to Governments for comments. Discussion in Plenary : 1150th , 1151st , 1152nd and 1153rd meetings (3 to 8 May 1972), 1164th meeting (24 May 1972), 1182nd , 1183rd , 1184th , 1185th and 1186th meetings (20 to 23 June 1972), 1188th and 1189th meetings (27 June 1972) 1191st , 1192nd and 1193th meetings (29 June to 3 July 1972) ILC Report, A/8710/Rev.1 (A/27/10), 1972, chap. III, paras. 54–69 Yearbook, 1972, vol. II","document_locator":"chap. III, paras","document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-cebb17607a4b326a6467ed86","section":"ilc_report"},"guide-entry-f51eb12f4122969614c10151":{"description":"24th session of the International Law Commission (1972) Report of the Working Group on the question of the protection and inviolability of diplomatic agents and other persons entitled to special protection under international law: draft articles on the prevention and punishment of crimes against diplomatic agents and other internationally protected persons A/CN.4/L.186 (in Yearbook, 1972, vol. I , 1182nd meeting (20 June 1972), 1185th and 1186th meetings (22 and 23 June 1972), 1188th and 1189th meetings (27 June 1972))","document_locator":null,"document_role":"primary_source","entry_id":"guide-entry-f51eb12f4122969614c10151","section":"working_group_or_subcommittee"},"guide-entry-fbb04a9a76a80c1ce876bdb7":{"description":"24th session of the International Law Commission (